Termux doesn't ship a real libstdc++, only a stub in the NDK sysroot
missing newer bionic symbols, so linking it in via the public Libs:
line of libraw.pc/libraw_r.pc breaks any consumer (e.g. rawtherapee)
that pulls in libraw via pkg-config. Replace it with the actual C++
runtime used on Android instead of dropping it.

--- a/libraw.pc.in
+++ b/libraw.pc.in
@@ -7,6 +7,6 @@
 Description: Raw image decoder library (non-thread-safe)
 Requires: @PACKAGE_REQUIRES@
 Version: @PACKAGE_VERSION@
-Libs: -L${libdir} -lraw -lstdc++@PC_OPENMP@
+Libs: -L${libdir} -lraw -lc++_shared@PC_OPENMP@
 Libs.private: @PACKAGE_LIBS_PRIVATE@
 Cflags: -I${includedir}/libraw -I${includedir}
--- a/libraw_r.pc.in
+++ b/libraw_r.pc.in
@@ -7,6 +7,6 @@
 Description: Raw image decoder library (thread-safe)
 Requires: @PACKAGE_REQUIRES@
 Version: @PACKAGE_VERSION@
-Libs: -L${libdir} -lraw_r -lstdc++@PC_OPENMP@
+Libs: -L${libdir} -lraw_r -lc++_shared@PC_OPENMP@
 Libs.private: @PACKAGE_LIBS_PRIVATE@
 Cflags: -I${includedir}/libraw -I${includedir}
